course: dictionary
lesson: 739
title: Bass: one word, several meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. Bass is a good example. The words around it tell you which meaning the writer wants. «The rhythm section is the bass and drums together, which hold the beat; the bass plays the low notes.» Drums and beat are music words, so bass here means the low part of the music.
explain: Look for clues in the sentence. «Anglers catch bass in lakes and the sea.» Anglers are people who go fishing, and lakes and the sea are where fish live, so bass here is a fish.
explain: Always check by swapping in your meaning. Does the sentence still make sense? If you say «the bass plays the low notes» and mean a fish, it falls apart. That tells you that you have picked the wrong meaning.
fact: Bass (said «base») means the lowest notes or sounds in music.
fact: A bass is a bass guitar or a double bass, a large string instrument that plays low notes.
fact: A bass is a man with a very deep singing voice.
fact: Bass (said «bas», to rhyme with «gas») is a kind of fish, and the plural is bass.
fact: Low pitch means slow vibrations: «Fast wobbles sound high and slow wobbles sound low.»
exercise: «The bass and drums together hold the beat.» What does bass mean here? | A loud drum | A kind of fish | *The lowest notes in music, played by the bass | A high, squeaky sound
exercise: «Anglers catch bass in lakes and the sea.» What is a bass in this sentence? | A deep singing voice | A string instrument | *A kind of fish | A low note
exercise: «A huge double bass booms, and a tiny ukulele squeaks.» Which instrument plays the lowest notes? | A squeaky toy | A tiny ukulele | *A huge double bass | A violin
test: «The bass plays the low notes.» How is bass said in this sentence? | *«base» | «bass», with a long hiss | «bas», to rhyme with «gas» | «bazz», like a buzz
test: «In the string family bigger instruments play lower: from highest to lowest they are violin, viola, cello and double bass.» Which instrument plays the lowest notes? | Cello | Viola | Violin | *Double bass
exam: Bass is spelled the same for the music word and the fish. How is the fish said? | «base» | «bazz», like a buzz | «bass», with a long hiss | *«bas», to rhyme with «gas»
